26 28 
.. 29 `concat` preflights typed headers and then streams ordinary chunks in argument
.. 30 order or performs a bounded coordinate merge with stable input ordering.
.. 31 Duplicate removal is cross-input and one-to-one. Indexed regions compose with
.. 32 position, record, and variant overlap rules.
.. 33 
.. 34 ```console
.. 35 rsomics-vcf concat chr1.vcf.gz chr2.vcf.gz -O z -o genome.vcf.gz
.. 36 rsomics-vcf concat -a -d exact cohort-a.bcf cohort-b.bcf -O b -o cohort.bcf
.. 37 rsomics-vcf concat -a -r chr1:1-1000000 chunk-a.vcf.gz chunk-b.vcf.gz
.. 38 ```
.. 39 
.. 40 Ligation reconciles complete phased diploid heterozygous genotypes across a
.. 41 chunk handoff and writes typed PQ and PS values. Each indexed chunk may contain
.. 42 records from one contig; separate files can advance to later contigs. Default
.. 43 ligation requires a perfect overlap, while `--ligate-warn` drops and reports
.. 44 unpaired overlap sites and `--ligate-force` retains them or permits disjoint
.. 45 chunks.
.. 46 
.. 47 Validated naive mode copies compatible BGZF VCF or BCF record frames without
.. 48 recompression. It rejects mixed encodings, incompatible headers or BCF
.. 49 dictionaries, malformed frames, CRC failures, missing canonical EOF blocks,
.. 50 and trailing bytes. Named output is transactional in every mode, and JSON
.. 51 summaries require a separate named variant destination.
.. 52 
